title: Aeternum Botnet Blockchain RPC Communication
id: 6f39590d-65e5-4372-a28d-1db2f0e7b41a
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects processes communicating with public Polygon blockchain RPC
    endpoints, the command-and-control channel of the Aeternum botnet
    loader (Unit 42, 2026): infected devices query attacker-controlled
    smart contracts through public RPC endpoints instead of a central
    C2 server.
references:
    - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/aeternum-blockchain-c2-analysis/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/08/11
tags:
    - attack.t1071
logsource:
    category: network_connection
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_domain:
        DestinationHostname|endswith:
            - 'polygon-rpc.com'
            - 'rpc-mainnet.matic.network'
            - 'rpc-mainnet.maticvigil.com'
            - 'polygon.llamarpc.com'
    selection_port:
        DestinationPort:
            - 8545
            - 8546
    condition: selection_domain or selection_port
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate wallets and DeFi applications using public RPC endpoints
    - Local development nodes bound to 8545/8546
level: medium
